1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,700
Good Morning, Youth Council. Caroline speaking.

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:08,220
Oh, hello, I'm interested in standing for election to the Youth Council

3
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:10,300
and I was told to give you a call.

4
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:15,630
That's good. Could I have your name, please? Yes, it's Roger Brown.

5
00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:19,158
Thank you. I'm Caroline, the Youth Council administrator.

6
00:00:19,158 --> 00:00:24,010
So do you know much about what the Council does, Roger?

7
00:00:24,010 --> 00:00:28,450
I've talked to Stephanie - I think she's the chair of the Council.

8
00:00:28,450 --> 00:00:31,440
That's right. And she told me a lot about it.

9
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:34,960
How it's a way for young people to discuss local issues

10
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:38,280
for example, and make suggestions to the town council.

11
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:44,200
That's what made me interested. Fine. Well let me take down some of your details.

12
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:46,860
First of all, how old are you

13
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:51,400
You know the Council is for young people aged from 13 to 18?

14
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:58,050
I've just turned 18. And where do you live, Roger? Well, that's a bit complicated.

15
00:00:58,050 --> 00:01:01,559
At the moment I'm looking for a flat to rent here,

16
00:01:01,559 --> 00:01:04,760
so I'm in a hostel from Monday to Friday

17
00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:07,620
I go back to my parents' place at the weekend.

18
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:13,000
OK, so where's the best place to send you some information about the Council?

19
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,190
Oh, to my parents' address, please.

20
00:01:15,190 --> 00:01:19,638
That's 17, Buckleigh Street-B-U-C-K-L-E. I-G-H Street,

21
00:01:19,638 --> 00:01:31,100
Stamford, Lincolnshire, though you don't really need the county

22
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:34,760
Oh, I know Stamford - it's a lovely town.

23
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:43,360
And what's the postcode? PE9 7QT Right, thank you

24
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:46,800
So are you working here, or are you a student?

25
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:50,062
I started studying at the university a couple of weeks ago,

26
00:01:50,062 --> 00:01:53,620
and I've got a part-time job for a few hours a week.

27
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:56,890
What do you do? Well, I've done several different things.

28
00:01:56,890 --> 00:01:59,827
I've just finished a short-term contract as a courier,

29
00:01:59,827 --> 00:02:04,070
and now I'm working as a waiter in one of the big hotels.

30
00:02:04,070 --> 00:02:07,300
Uhuh. That can't leave you much time for studying!

31
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:12,000
Oh, it's not too bad. I managed to fit it all in. What are you studying?

32
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,710
My ambition is to go into parliament eventually, so my major subject is politics.

33
00:02:17,710 --> 00:02:20,960
That's partly why I think the Youth Council is important

34
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:23,050
and want to be a part of it.

35
00:02:23,050 --> 00:02:26,940
And I suppose you're also taking a minor subject, aren't you

36
00:02:27,220 --> 00:02:30,140
I know a lot of people study economics too.

37
00:02:30,140 --> 00:02:35,430
I chose history. To be honest, I'm not finding it as interesting as I expected!

38
00:02:35,430 --> 00:02:40,120
OK, so with your studying and your part-time job

39
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:43,140
do you have time for any other interests or hobbies?

40
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:46,120
Well, I spend quite a lot of time cycling

41
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:50,041
both around town to get to university and to work,

42
00:02:50,041 --> 00:02:53,310
and also long-distance, from here to London, for instance.

43
00:02:53,310 --> 00:02:56,550
That's pretty impressive! Anything else?

44
00:02:56,550 --> 00:02:59,055
For relaxation I'm also keen on the cinema -

45
00:02:59,055 --> 00:03:04,690
I used to go at least once a week, but I can't manage to go so often now.

46
00:03:04,690 --> 00:03:09,200
Right. Are you sure you'll have enough time for the Youth Council?

47
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:13,260
Yes, I've worked out that I can afford to reduce my hours at work

48
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:14,400
and that will make the time.

49
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:19,600
So is there any particular aspect of the Youth Council's work that appeals to you, Roger?

50
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:22,320
Well my sister is blind

51
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:26,275
so I'm particularly interested in working with disabled young people,

52
00:03:26,275 --> 00:03:30,280
to try and improve the quality of their lives.

53
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:36,740
That's great. Well, the best way to get involved is to be nominated by some people who you know.

54
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:40,360
Right. Can you tell me how to set about organising that?

55
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:44,030
You should talk to Jeffrey, our Elections Officer.

56
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:49,050
I can arrange a meeting in the council office with him, if you like. Yes, please.

57
00:03:49,050 --> 00:03:52,720
He'll be here next Monday, if that suits you.

58
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:57,900
That's the 14th, isn't it? Yes. I can manage late afternoon.

59
00:03:57,900 --> 00:04:03,100
Would you like to suggest a time? He generally leaves around 5.30.

60
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:08,760
Well, would 4.30 be OK? My last class finishes at 4

61
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:11,050
so I'd have plenty of time to get to your office.

62
00:04:11,050 --> 00:04:16,950
Right, that's fine. Oh, and could I have a phone number we can contact you on?

63
00:04:16,950 --> 00:04:25,560
Yes, my mobile number's 07788 136711.

64
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:29,650
Thank you. Well, well look forward to seeing you next week.

65
00:04:29,650 --> 00:04:32,800
Thanks very much. Goodbye. Bye.
